    <amat:TreasuryStockPolicyPolicyTextBlock contextRef="c-1" id="f-977">We record common stock repurchased and held as treasury stock under the cost method using the first-in, first-out method. Upon reissuance of treasury stock, amounts in excess of the acquisition cost are credited to additional paid in capital. If we reissue treasury stock at an amount below our acquisition cost and additional paid in capital associated with prior treasury stock transactions is insufficient to cover the difference between the acquisition cost and the reissue price, this difference is recorded against retained earnings.</amat:TreasuryStockPolicyPolicyTextBlock>
